 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration allows retrieving scrape targets from [Scaleway Instances API](https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/instance/#path-servers-list-servers).
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # project is the id of the Scaleway project to discover instances from.
+    # Either project or organization must be set.
+    #
+  - project: "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"
+
+    # organization is the id of the Scaleway organization to discover instances from.
+    # Either project or organization must be set.
+    #
+    # organization: "..."
+
+    # secret_key is the Scaleway API secret key used for authentication.
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/identity-and-access-management/iam/how-to/create-api-keys/
+    #
+    secret_key: "..."
+
+    # api_url is an optional Scaleway API server to query.
+    # By default, https://api.scaleway.com is used.
+    #
+    # api_url: "https://api.scaleway.com"
+
+    # zones is an optional list of Scaleway zones to discover instances from.
+    # By default, all the known Scaleway zones are queried.
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/#regions-and-zones
+    #
+    # zones: ["fr-par-1", "fr-par-2"]
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from. By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<public_ip>:<port>`, where `<public_ip>` is the public IPv4 address of the instance, or `<private_ip>:<port>` if the instance has no public IP.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the id of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the zone the instance runs in
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the commercial type of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_state`: the state of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project`: the id of the project the instance belongs to
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization`: the id of the organization the instance belongs to
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: the comma-separated list of tags of the instance
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
